241
00:14:35,400 --> 00:14:40,000
I'll summon the all-powerful Ixodia,
the Forbidden One, and obliterate Yugi.

242
00:14:40,320 --> 00:14:41,457
Yugi, watch out for...

243
00:14:41,540 --> 00:14:42,517
Silence, Wheeler.

244
00:14:42,600 --> 00:14:45,040
Or say goodbye to your red eyes.

245
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:49,520
To start off, I place two
cards face down on the field.

246
00:14:51,180 --> 00:14:54,700
Next, I summon Beta the
Magnet Warrior in attack mode.

247
00:14:57,860 --> 00:15:00,100
Can you handle my newest monster?

248
00:15:00,380 --> 00:15:01,680
What is that, Bob?

249
00:15:01,860 --> 00:15:04,417
It's obviously a big yellow
magnet with eyeballs.

250
00:15:04,500 --> 00:15:06,377
That's what you call a dual monster.

251
00:15:06,460 --> 00:15:09,840
The dual disc renders the
cards in holographic 3D.

252
00:15:11,140 --> 00:15:15,800
My first card will be
just what I suspected.

253
00:15:16,860 --> 00:15:19,480
Graceful Charity lets me draw three cards.

254
00:15:21,120 --> 00:15:22,860
And I discard two.

255
00:15:23,440 --> 00:15:24,270
Perfect.

256
00:15:24,353 --> 00:15:25,849
The third piece of Exodia.

257
00:15:25,960 --> 00:15:27,640
Only two more pieces left.

258
00:15:28,060 --> 00:15:31,160
If you only knew what
was in my hand waiting,

259
00:15:31,360 --> 00:15:36,320
you'd forfeit now and relinquish
your rare dark magician. Never.

260
00:15:36,640 --> 00:15:38,437
I may not know what's in your hand,

261
00:15:38,520 --> 00:15:40,737
but my trap card Light of Intervention

262
00:15:40,820 --> 00:15:43,297
reveals all your hidden
monsters on the field.

263
00:15:43,380 --> 00:15:45,909
There will be no surprise
attacks from you.

264
00:15:46,680 --> 00:15:47,510
Hmm.

265
00:15:47,820 --> 00:15:48,717
Doesn't matter.

266
00:15:48,800 --> 00:15:52,500
Stone Statue of the
Aztecs in Defense Mode!

267
00:15:56,600 --> 00:15:59,659
All he's done so far is
draw cards and play defense.

268
00:15:59,900 --> 00:16:01,841
He must be waiting for something.

269
00:16:02,020 --> 00:16:05,520
It's time for your Stone
Statue to crumble now!

270
00:16:06,620 --> 00:16:07,960
By Battle City rules,

271
00:16:08,160 --> 00:16:13,200
I sacrifice my weaker Magnet Warrior
to summon the almighty Perfomet!

272
00:16:14,420 --> 00:16:18,361
And he is able to bring forth
Gazelle, the King of Mythical Beasts!

273
00:16:18,800 --> 00:16:19,630
That's not all!

274
00:16:19,713 --> 00:16:23,120
Now I use Polymerization
to fuse them together!

275
00:16:31,020 --> 00:16:34,300
Forming Chimera, the
flying mythical beast!

276
00:16:37,520 --> 00:16:38,920
On my next turn,

277
00:16:39,100 --> 00:16:43,957
my all-powerful Chimera will erode your
stone statue into tiny pieces of rubble.

278
00:16:44,040 --> 00:16:44,870
Then,

279
00:16:44,953 --> 00:16:47,957
according to Battle City rules, once
you have no monsters left on the field,

280
00:16:48,040 --> 00:16:49,917
I can attack your life points directly.

281
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:51,657
Forget about what's on the field.

282
00:16:51,740 --> 00:16:53,564
Worry about what's in his hand.

283
00:16:53,680 --> 00:16:54,621
Very impressive.

284
00:16:54,800 --> 00:16:57,977
But you'll need more than
that to scare off the hunter.

285
00:16:58,060 --> 00:16:58,890
Listen, you.

286
00:16:58,973 --> 00:17:01,175
This guy's got a plan to wipe you out.

287
00:17:01,260 --> 00:17:03,557
Check out the grin on
that other kisser of his.

288
00:17:03,640 --> 00:17:06,017
This is exactly what
the old creep did to me.

289
00:17:06,100 --> 00:17:07,877
He's got something in
his hand that's gonna...

290
00:17:07,960 --> 00:17:08,877
Silence, Wheeler.

291
00:17:08,960 --> 00:17:11,917
One more word out of you and say
goodbye to your red eyes forever.

292
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:16,460
I'll end my turn by placing this
card face down on the field.

293
00:17:17,040 --> 00:17:19,320
I predict another graceful charity.

294
00:17:21,400 --> 00:17:22,400
Imagine that.

295
00:17:22,540 --> 00:17:23,460
I was correct.

296
00:17:23,780 --> 00:17:28,040
I draw three more cards and discard two.

297
00:17:28,420 --> 00:17:30,949
How does he know what
card he'll draw next?

298
00:17:32,380 --> 00:17:33,210
Excellent.

299
00:17:33,293 --> 00:17:35,060
I now have four Exodia pieces.

300
00:17:35,320 --> 00:17:39,497
I only need one more to summon the beast
that will obliterate Yugi in one attack.

301
00:17:39,580 --> 00:17:42,920
He's about to lose his
Dark Magician forever!

302
00:17:46,160 --> 00:17:48,880
This duelist is battling
well against Yugi.

303
00:17:49,260 --> 00:17:50,520
But who is he?

304
00:17:50,780 --> 00:17:53,540
What info do we have on him? Very little.

305
00:17:53,700 --> 00:17:57,317
He wasn't listed in your tournament
database until about a week ago.

306
00:17:57,400 --> 00:17:58,230
What?

307
00:17:58,313 --> 00:17:59,143
How's that possible?

308
00:17:59,240 --> 00:18:01,717
He must have hacked into the
system and added himself.

309
00:18:01,800 --> 00:18:02,682
That's illegal!

310
00:18:02,840 --> 00:18:04,664
He calls himself a rare hunter.

311
00:18:04,900 --> 00:18:06,260
We'll disqualify him!

312
00:18:06,660 --> 00:18:07,657
Right, Seto?

313
00:18:07,740 --> 00:18:12,480
Wait, rare hunters, they took my bait.

314
00:18:13,500 --> 00:18:15,880
Mokuba, it's just as I planned.

315
00:18:19,740 --> 00:18:22,328
Yugi, your dark magician
is as good as mine.

316
00:18:24,740 --> 00:18:28,446
Once I've assembled all five
pieces of the all-powerful Exodia,

317
00:18:28,660 --> 00:18:30,180
this hunt will be over.

318
00:18:30,380 --> 00:18:34,877
And with the help of some invisible
ink and my x-ray contact lens,

319
00:18:34,960 --> 00:18:38,780
I'll know exactly what
card I'll be drawing next!

320
00:18:41,260 --> 00:18:42,560
Just what I need!

321
00:18:42,760 --> 00:18:47,117
It's the final piece of the puzzle, the
left arm of Exodia the Forbidden One!

322
00:18:47,200 --> 00:18:48,997
When I draw it on my next turn,

323
00:18:49,080 --> 00:18:52,520
I'll summon my most powerful
creature and obliterate Yugi!

324
00:18:54,160 --> 00:18:56,260
Now I'll strengthen my defenses!

325
00:18:58,140 --> 00:19:01,600
To protect me, Gear Golem
the Moving Fortress!

326
00:19:04,400 --> 00:19:09,177
Even your Chimera is not powerful enough
to destroy it What are you going to do now,

327
00:19:09,260 --> 00:19:10,090
Yugi?

328
00:19:10,173 --> 00:19:12,760
You can't beat me if you
can't get by my defenses

329
00:19:14,060 --> 00:19:18,217
You may be protecting your life points
with fortresses and stone walls,

330
00:19:18,300 --> 00:19:20,677
Rare Hunter But in order
for you to win this duel,

331
00:19:20,760 --> 00:19:24,137
you must attack me eventually
So what are you waiting for?

332
00:19:24,220 --> 00:19:28,340
Oh, you'll find out soon
enough, Yugi So go ahead,

333
00:19:28,700 --> 00:19:32,818
make your move The hunter will strike
his prey when the time is right.

334
00:19:34,360 --> 00:19:35,190
Hey, you!

335
00:19:35,860 --> 00:19:36,690
Hold it!

336
00:19:36,773 --> 00:19:39,300
I can't stand by and watch this. No way!

337
00:19:39,520 --> 00:19:42,157
I won't let you lose your
dark magician for me.

338
00:19:42,240 --> 00:19:43,416
That's enough, Joey!

339
00:19:44,540 --> 00:19:47,560
You must not reveal the
rare hunter's strategy.

340
00:19:47,900 --> 00:19:49,280
I will defeat him.

341
00:19:49,500 --> 00:19:52,617
You're my friend, Joey, and
I'm fighting this duel for you,

342
00:19:52,700 --> 00:19:54,347
just as you would do for me.

343
00:19:55,560 --> 00:19:56,390
You're right.

344
00:19:57,260 --> 00:20:01,319
Do you remember the time Weevil
threw my Exodia cards into the ocean?

345
00:20:01,500 --> 00:20:04,337
You risked your life to
try to get my cards back.

346
00:20:04,420 --> 00:20:07,417
Not just because Exodia is the
most powerful card in the game,

347
00:20:07,500 --> 00:20:09,600
but because I was a friend in need.

348
00:20:11,240 --> 00:20:12,880
Exodia! That's it!

349
00:20:13,220 --> 00:20:18,017
This Rare Hunter is drawing cards until
he can assemble all five pieces of Exodia.

350
00:20:18,100 --> 00:20:19,140
I'm on to you.

351
00:20:19,340 --> 00:20:21,340
I know your strategy, Rare Hunter.

352
00:20:23,080 --> 00:20:26,139
You're planning to summon
Exodia, the Forbidden One!

353
00:20:26,300 --> 00:20:27,660
Oh, no!

354
00:20:28,020 --> 00:20:29,040
How does he know?

355
00:20:30,060 --> 00:20:30,890
Hooray!

356
00:20:31,460 --> 00:20:32,297
Thank you, Joey.

357
00:20:32,380 --> 00:20:36,017
You allowed me to figure out his strategy
without actually telling it to me.

358
00:20:36,100 --> 00:20:36,930
Oh, yeah!

359
00:20:38,160 --> 00:20:40,357
Just because you figured out my strategy

360
00:20:40,440 --> 00:20:43,087
doesn't mean you can
stop me from succeeding.

361
00:20:43,400 --> 00:20:47,400
Everyone knows Exodia's the most
powerful creature in Duel Monsters.

362
00:20:47,520 --> 00:20:50,120
How will you stop the unstoppable Exodia?

363
00:20:50,880 --> 00:20:51,710
True.

364
00:20:51,793 --> 00:20:53,297
No one has ever defeated Exodia.

365
00:20:53,380 --> 00:20:57,700
But in order to win back Joey's Red-Eyes
Black Dragon, I'll be the first.

366
00:20:57,960 --> 00:20:58,920
Give up, Yugi.

367
00:20:59,160 --> 00:21:00,640
My hunt is over.
